%
(rs274ngc-basics.ngc)
(Structure and modal behaviour. Composed to the line format of NIST RS274/NGC and its)
(LinuxCNC descendant - NOT captured from any application. See the README.)
(preamble: XY plane, inches, cutter comp off, tool length offset off, work offset 1,)
(canned cycles off, absolute distance mode, feed per minute)
N10 G17 G20 G40 G49 G54 G80 G90 G94
N15 G0 X0 Y0 ; a semicolon comments out the rest of the line
N20 M3 S800 (spindle on; parens comment out to the matching paren)
N30 G1 X1.250 Y0 F60 (establishes motion mode G1 and the feed rate)
N40 Y1.250 (modal motion: axis words only, the G word is omitted)
N50 X0.000 (modal motion)
N60 Y0 (modal motion - square closed)
N70 G4 P0.25 (dwell in seconds; non-modal, so it does not change the motion mode)
N80 X0.625 Y0.625 (still modal G1, at the feed set on N30)
N90 G0 X0 Y0 (rapid; the motion mode is now G0)
N100 M5 (spindle/laser off)
N110 M2 (program end: plane, units, distance mode, feed mode, spindle and motion mode all reset)
%
